{"lines": ["In 1967, at Cambridge, a graduate student named Jocelyn Bell was reading miles of paper chart from a new radio telescope.", "She noticed a strange signal, a pulse that repeated with almost perfect regularity, about every one point three three seven seconds.", "On November 28th, 1967, she pinned it down.", "Natural objects were not supposed to keep time that well.", "The team jokingly named it LGM-1, for \"little green men.\"", "Bell and her supervisor, Antony Hewish, considered the idea, though they did not truly believe it.", "They asked how one announces something like that responsibly, and who to tell first.", "Then she found a similar signal in another part of the sky, and the answer changed.", "It was a rapidly rotating neutron star, the first pulsar ever recognized.", "Hewish received the 1974 Nobel Prize, and Bell did not. In 2018 she won the three-million-dollar Breakthrough Prize."], "words": [["In", 0.0, 0.08], ["1967,", 0.08, 0.34], ["at", 1.88, 2.12], ["Cambridge,", 2.12, 2.34], ["a", 3.14, 3.32], ["graduate", 3.32, 3.68], ["student", 3.68, 4.14], ["named", 4.14, 4.62], ["Jocelyn", 4.62, 5.26], ["Bell", 5.26, 5.46], ["was", 5.46, 6.06], ["reading", 6.06, 6.32], ["miles", 6.32, 6.76], ["of", 6.76, 7.06], ["paper", 7.06, 7.28], ["chart", 7.28, 7.7], ["from", 7.7, 8.3], ["a", 8.3, 8.4], ["new", 8.4, 8.58], ["radio", 8.58, 8.96], ["telescope.", 8.96, 9.68], ["She", 10.26, 10.46], ["noticed", 10.46, 10.74], ["a", 10.74, 11.04], ["strange", 11.04, 11.36], ["signal,", 11.36, 12.0], ["a", 12.48, 12.6], ["pulse", 12.6, 12.82], ["that", 12.82, 13.16], ["repeated", 13.16, 13.44], ["with", 13.44, 13.8], ["almost", 13.8, 14.06], ["perfect", 14.06, 14.48], ["regularity,", 14.48, 15.56], ["about", 15.88, 16.12], ["every", 16.12, 16.36], ["one", 16.36, 16.62], ["point", 16.62, 16.88], ["three", 16.88, 17.14], ["three", 17.14, 17.4], ["seven", 17.4, 17.66], ["seconds.", 17.66, 18.46], ["On", 19.08, 19.16], ["November", 19.16, 19.42], ["28th,", 19.42, 20.66], 